Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(update): check the Harmony fork's GitHub releases
 for -harmony builds

Fork builds are versioned <upstream>-harmony.<n>. The official update server treats
that as a pre-release of <upstream> and offers the official APK, which cannot be
installed over an APK signed with a different key. When the running version matches
the fork pattern, UpdateChecker now lists the fork's GitHub releases, compares the
(major, minor, patch, harmony) tuple, and offers the matching -arm64-v8a.apk (universal
as fallback). The release-notes link follows the same rule.
